course: dictionary
lesson: 454
title: Words that begin or appear
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word arise means to begin or to appear, usually a problem, a question or a chance. «If a problem arises, tell an adult» means if a problem happens, tell an adult. The clue is in the words around it: a problem is something that starts.
explain: Arise is a verb, so its forms change: arise, arises, arose, arisen, arising. In «the Ming and the Mughals ... arose later», arose is the past form. It means came into being, so the Ming and the Mughals began after the other rulers.
explain: «Feelings often arise without being chosen» means feelings begin or appear without you deciding them. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Feelings often begin without being chosen» still makes sense. In old stories and poems, «Arise!» means «Get up!», so always check the clues.
fact: Arise means to begin or appear, usually a problem, question or chance.
fact: In old stories and poems, «arise» means to get up or stand up.
fact: The forms of arise are: arise, arises, arose, arisen, arising.
fact: Useful phrases are «if the need arises» and «arise from».
fact: «Arose» is the past form, as in «the Ming arose later».
exercise: «If a problem arises, tell an adult.» What does arises mean here? | *It begins or happens | It is lost forever | It is hidden under a table | It gets up from a chair
exercise: «Questions that arise from the experiment» are questions that... | *make you think of new things | are written in old books | are always easy to answer | are sung in a song
exercise: In an old poem, a voice cries «Arise!» What does the voice want? | *To get up | To sing a quiet song | To leave the room forever | To go to sleep
test: Which word is the past form of arise? | arising | arisen | arises | *arose
test: In «Feelings often arise without being chosen», what does arise mean? | *Begin or appear | Be chosen | Disappear | Stand up
exam: Choose the best word: «If the need ___, we will help.» | arising | arise | arisen | *arises
